//  - Cache-friendly spatial blocking (tiling) in i and j using noarr::into_blocks,
//    guarded by a runtime check so we only tile when the interior size is
//    divisible by the chosen tile sizes.
//  - The blocking is done independently for each time step; sweeps over A->B
//    and B->A for a given time step are still globally ordered as in the
//    original code (first complete A->B over the whole domain, then complete
//    B->A over the whole domain), so the numerical scheme is unchanged.
